    "summary": "Added SMALLEST_CHANGE_RULE (the build ladder, with the insrc analyzer for the 'already in the codebase' rung and insrc's limits: the Task or LLD is the spec, named tests stay required, validation, error handling, security and accessibility are never cut) and SMALLEST_SHAPE_RULE (the design counterpart) to scope-prompts.ts, with a Ponytail (MIT) credit comment. The build rule is a new 'The smallest complete change' section in the implement template (via a smallestChangeRule placeholder) and in renderStandaloneImplementPrompt; the design rule is in the alternatives.enumerate prompt before ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md at the repository root credits Ponytail with its link and its MIT licence text copied from upstream. Tests extend the render and adjacent-scope tests and add a notice test.",
